  "body": "Sibling left alone by the Usage fix for Desktop's Code tab sessions (Session.App, CyberCaius on Discord).\n\nA Claude Code session that Claude Desktop's Code tab ran is in ~/.claude/projects and is now listed with `App: \"claude-desktop\"`; `GatewayKeys`, `MergeExternal` and the stats' native keys treat the gateway's `claude-desktop|<id>` record as the same session.\n\n`sessions.NativeIDs` / `nativeIDsWith` (internal/sessions/manage.go), used by `/api/sessions/manage` and `/api/sessions/delete`, only looks at files whose agent was asked for. Asked for `claude-desktop`, it doesn't look at Claude Code's files, so on the Sessions page a Code tab session the gateway also saw can show under Claude Desktop as a gateway-only session beside its native row under Claude Code.\n\nA fix reads the entrypoint (`state.Entry`) of `claude` files when `claude-desktop` is asked for, as Raft's files are read when `pi` is asked for. Claude Code's ids come from the file name (`idInFile` is false), so the claude files' parses may not be fresh in the quick path; that needs care.\n\nNot reproduced with a real Desktop Code tab: this machine has no Code tab transcripts.",
