   "body": "Fixed on [fix/4333-desktop-native-session-ids](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/4333-desktop-native-session-ids), commit [ed2c1bf9](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/ed2c1bf945e30fe78d692f081780aee221c4aa3c), based on upstream `ed0ab567`.\n\nWhen Desktop IDs are requested, `NativeIDs` now also reads Claude Code files and recognizes the `claude-desktop` and `claude-desktop-3p` entrypoints. The quick path reads a fresh glance when the cached parse is pending, and the management list uses those IDs as the count already does, so a matching Desktop gateway row is not shown as a second session. Ordinary Claude CLI and Raft coverage is retained.\n\nSynthetic JSONL regressions for both entrypoints fail on the base and pass after the change; they cover cold and changed quick reads, Desktop-only lookup and CLI separation. A real `/api/sessions/manage` handler test verifies both counts and rows. Focused sessions/GUI tests pass under `-race`, and scoped vet plus `go build -tags nogui ./...` pass. No real Desktop transcript was available.\n\nThe full sessions race run was not green: its cache/test race and two allocation-budget failures also reproduce on the unchanged base; a fourth prefix-hash failure could not be reproduced on either tree, and its original detail was not retained. Full nogui and Windows runtime testing were not done. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
